  <h2>2. What the service does</h2>
  <p>
    You register a monitor for a scheduled job. Your job calls a unique ping URL each time it runs. If a ping
    does not arrive within the interval and grace period you configured, or if your job reports a failure, we
    record an incident and email you. When the job pings successfully again, we email you that it recovered.
    We also keep a history of pings and a per-day uptime record.
  </p>
  <p>
    That is the whole product. Stablemate watches for the <em>absence</em> of a signal you send us — it does not
    run your jobs, cannot fix them, and cannot tell you anything your jobs do not report.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Your account</h2>
