      choose which <%= free_limit %> stay active; the rest are <em>suspended</em>, not deleted, and come back if
      you upgrade again.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cancelling in the Stripe billing portal</strong> (Billing &rarr; Manage payment details) takes effect
      on the schedule Stripe&rsquo;s portal is configured for &mdash; normally <strong>at the end of the period you
      have already paid for</strong>. You keep Pro until then, and your plan drops to Free when Stripe tells us
      the subscription has ended.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Either way, cancelling never deletes your monitors or their history. To delete your data, delete your
    account (section 9).
  </p>

  <h3>If a payment fails, or a subscription ends unexpectedly</h3>
  <p>
    Your plan drops to Free, but nothing is suspended straight away &mdash; a billing blip must never silently stop
    your monitoring. Instead, if you are over the Free allowance, you get <strong><%= grace_days %> days</strong> to
